  "description": "ENOXOV crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R -3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C60 H112 Ce6 O32. From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce1B (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce1A (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce1I (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce1K (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce1J (Ce) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.764-3.770 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 117.27-118.35°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C60H112Ce6O32. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Ce(IV).",
